WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:21.240
I would like to talk to you about why many E-off projects fail and I really think that

00:21.240 --> 00:26.400
the most important thing of it is that we stop listening to patients and one of the

00:26.400 --> 00:30.460
things we did at Robert University is we appointed a Chief Listening Officer, not on

00:30.460 --> 00:36.120
a very scientific way, she puts up a little cup of coffee or a cup of tea and asks patients,

00:36.120 --> 00:42.460
family, relatives, what's up? How could we help you? And we think, we like to think that

00:42.460 --> 00:47.920
this is one of the major problems why all, maybe not all, but most of the E-off projects

00:47.920 --> 00:53.280
fail since we stopped listening. This is my weighing skill. It's a very simple thing,

00:53.280 --> 01:00.280
it's got one nut, on, off, and every morning I hop on it and yes, I got a challenge, as

01:00.280 --> 01:06.640
you might see, and I put my challenge on 95 kilograms, but the thing is that it's made

01:06.640 --> 01:13.040
this simple, that whenever I hop on, it sends my data to Google Health as well and it's

01:13.040 --> 01:19.320
collected by my general petitioner as well, so he can see what's my problem in weight,

01:19.320 --> 01:25.400
not on the very moment that I need cardiologic support or something like it, but also looking

01:25.400 --> 01:31.360
back for it. But there's another thing, as some of you might know, I got more than 4,000

01:31.360 --> 01:36.600
followers on Twitter, so every morning I hop on my weighing skill and before I'm in my

01:36.600 --> 01:42.400
car people start talking to me, I think you need a light lunch today, Leshan. But that's

01:42.400 --> 01:47.820
the nicest thing that could happen since this is peer pressure. Peer pressure used to help

01:47.820 --> 01:54.960
patients, since this could be used for B-Stas, it could be used to stop smoking for patients,

01:54.960 --> 01:59.800
but on the other hand it also could be used to get people from out of their chairs and

01:59.800 --> 02:05.780
try to work together in some kind of gaming activity to get more control of their health.

02:05.780 --> 02:10.720
And as of next week, it will be soon available, there will be this little blood pressure meter

02:10.720 --> 02:16.820
connected to an iPhone or something or other, and people will be able from their homes to

02:16.820 --> 02:21.980
take their blood pressure, send it in to their doctor and eventually share it to others,

02:21.980 --> 02:26.860
for instance, for over a hundred dollars. And this is the point where patients get into

02:26.860 --> 02:32.660
position and can collect not only their own control again, being captain of the ownership,

02:32.660 --> 02:38.740
but also can help us in healthcare due to the challenges that we're facing, like healthcare,

02:38.740 --> 02:44.160
cost explosion, double demand and things like that. Make techniques that's easy to use and

02:44.160 --> 02:48.320
start with this to embrace patients in the team. And you could do this with techniques

02:48.320 --> 02:53.600
like this, but also by crowdsourcing. And one of the things we did, I would like to

02:53.600 --> 02:55.960
share with you, introduced by a little video.

03:44.160 --> 04:11.200
We all got navigation controls in our car.

04:11.200 --> 04:16.400
We maybe even got it in our cell phone. We perfectly know where all the ADMs are, just

04:16.400 --> 04:21.320
about the city of Maastricht. The other thing is we know where all the gas stations are.

04:21.320 --> 04:27.360
And sure, we could find fast food chains. But where would be the nearest AED to help

04:27.360 --> 04:33.120
this patient? We asked around and nobody knew. Nobody knew where the nearest life-saving

04:33.120 --> 04:38.680
AED was to obtain, right now. So what we did, we crowdsourced to the Netherlands and we

04:38.680 --> 04:43.820
set up a website and asked the crowd, if you see an AED, please submit it. Tell us

04:43.820 --> 04:49.560
where it is. Tell us when it's open, since sometimes in office hours it's closed of course.

04:49.560 --> 04:53.160
And over 10,000 AEDs in the Netherlands already have been submitted.

04:53.160 --> 04:58.160
The next step we took was find applications for it. And we built an iPad application.

04:58.160 --> 05:03.240
We made an application for layer, augmented reality, to find these AEDs. And whenever

05:03.240 --> 05:08.280
you were in a city like Maastricht and somebody collapsed, you can use your iPhone. And within

05:08.280 --> 05:13.160
the next weeks, also on your Microsoft cell phone. To find the nearest AED, which can

05:13.160 --> 05:18.960
save lives. And as of today, we would like to introduce this not only as AED for you,

05:18.960 --> 05:23.360
which is the product called, but also AED for us. And we would like to start this on

05:23.360 --> 05:28.720
a worldwide level. And asking all colleagues of us in the rest of the world, college universities

05:28.720 --> 05:35.400
to help us to find and work and act like a hub, to crowdsource all these AEDs around

05:35.400 --> 05:39.680
the world. That whenever you are on a holiday and somebody collapses, might it be your own

05:39.680 --> 05:44.600
relative or someone just in front of you, you can find this. The other thing we would

05:44.600 --> 05:49.520
like to ask is companies also all over the world that will be able to help us validate

05:49.520 --> 05:55.480
these AEDs. This might be courier services or cable guys, for instance, just to see whether

05:55.480 --> 06:01.460
the AED that's submitted still is in place. So please help us on this one and try to make

06:01.460 --> 06:04.880
not only health a little bit better, but take control of it. Thank you.

